      "content": {
        "heading": "The Golden Rules of Signs",
        "bullets": [
          "Formula: 1/f = 1/v - 1/u",
          "Object Distance (u): ALWAYS Negative (-)",
          "Convex Lens Focal Length (f): ALWAYS Positive (+)",
          "Concave Lens Focal Length (f): ALWAYS Negative (-)"
        ],
        "imageUrl": "/images/convex_vs_concave_lens_signs.svg"
      },
      "teacherScript": "The Lens formula is 1 over f equals 1 over v minus 1 over u. Remember these golden rules: Object distance u is ALWAYS negative. Convex lens focal length f is ALWAYS positive. Concave lens focal length f is ALWAYS negative.",
